      "writtenOn": "2023-07-14T16:48:50Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "We can\u0027t easily reference `rust.*` from `cc` due to a circular dependency. This isn\u0027t in itself a deal breaker since we could refactor this out into `LinkableInterface`.\n\nHowever, the functions which calculate the stem, `cc.libraryDecorator.getLibName` and `rust.libraryDecorator.getStem`, require `cc.BaseModuleContext` and `rust.ModuleContext` respectively. I don\u0027t believe the module context (even the base `android.*` equivalent) is available at this point.\n\nThe final output filename may have other context-related aspects that go into it (for example Rust will produce a different DylibSuffix depending on the target toolchain, https://source.corp.google.com/h/android/platform/superproject/main/+/main:build/soong/rust/config/darwin_host.go;l\u003d94-96).\n\nI think this is why the existing code above does a similar reconstruction from `libPath.Base()`.\n \nHere, the specific `.rlib-std` string isn\u0027t load-bearing; it can be anything since all it does is serve to differentiate the variant filenames in the vendor snapshot.\n\nMarking this potentially resolved but feel free to reopen if you disagree.",
      "parentUuid": "b2501ee5_102cadc5",
      "revId": "538b59c8f7f29308274ed799a124fb9dfeba4ebe",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
